From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:28:28 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] misc: egisfp: Add power and interrupt control for the Egis
 EC617
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Not for upstream.

The EC617 fingerprint sensor of the Xperia 10 VI sits on an SPI bus
that TrustZone owns: its trusted application talks to it, and Linux only
powers it, resets it and reports its interrupt. Give userspace those
through a misc device, with an eventfd for the interrupt, so that a
libfprint driver can run the sensor through the trusted application.

The binding is a development one and the uapi is not stable.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
